sub:assertion {
<https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/levin-2023-competency-13> a <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim>;
    dc:description "The authors suggest that because competency hides genetic deficiencies from selection, a positive-feedback ratchet arises in which evolution increasingly improves the problem-solving competency (intelligence) of its cellular material rather than the structural genome, a possible driver for scaling intelligence in morphological and other spaces.";
    dc:type "mechanism";
    <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "An intelligence ratchet locks evolution into improving cellular competency";
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Shreesha L, Levin M, “Cellular Competency during Development Alters Evolutionary Dynamics in an Artificial Embryogeny Model”, Entropy (Basel, Switzerland) (2023), doi:10.3390/e25010131; section “4. Discussion › 4.6. Where the Hard Work Is Done: An Intelligence Ratchet”. Scope: Evolution of developmental systems; inferred from the 1D artificial embryogeny model"
}
